This skill's subject is consulting current third-party documentation and
implementation code, so its behavior cases cannot be measured offline.
Presence of this file makes scripts/shuhari_staged_targets.sh evaluate them
with gpt-5.5, medium reasoning, and network access in the isolated sandbox.

The repository's default 5.6 models cannot use the web-search tool directly.
They answer

    403 Forbidden: Selected provider is forbidden

and falls back to memory or to a direct API call, often without saying so.
`gpt-5.5` searches normally, checked with the same question from the same
empty directory, so the skill uses it as both the bounded runtime fallback and
the behavior-evaluation model. Ordinary behavior cases and all trigger checks
retain the repository's default offline policy.
